The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (ret) {
    unpin_user_pages(pages, nr_pages);
    return ret;
}
```
Reason:
When `sg_alloc_table_from_pages` fails, the code correctly unpins the user pages to release page references, but fails to free the dynamically allocated `pages` array (allocated via `kvcalloc` inside `io_pin_pages`). This causes a memory leak because the array is never released.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (ret) {
    unpin_user_pages(pages, nr_pages);
    kvfree(pages);
    return ret;
}
```
Reason:
Adding `kvfree(pages)` ensures that the dynamically allocated page array is freed when `sg_alloc_table_from_pages` fails, preventing the memory leak. The `unpin_user_pages` call releases the individual page references, and `kvfree` releases the array itself.

